"1189",""
"1190",""
"1191",""
"1192",""
"1193","On the authority of a man from the Ansar, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the funeral of a man from the Ansar. When we returned, we encountered the messenger of a woman from Quraysh, who said: ""So-and-so invites you and those with you to a meal."" So he turned back, sat down, and we sat with him. The food was brought. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand [to eat], and the people placed their hands. They watched the Prophet ﷺ, and when a morsel was in his mouth he could not swallow it. So they restrained their hands to see what the Prophet ﷺ would do. He took his morsel and spat it out, saying: ""I find the meat of a sheep taken without the permission of its owners. Feed it to the captives."""
